{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nReframed 2026-08-19 (operator session): the original framing — one contradiction shipping through\n12 plan-review rounds — was an instance of a broader defect: **the code-review gate cannot block\nconsequential test-sufficiency findings, because the code-v3 impact model discards the verifier's\nown user-reach judgments.**\n\nExemplar (kept as the fire case): Gerrit commit `8eadb4fbc5` shipped, in one diff, a contract\ndeclaring \"``stale>0`` alone is an allowed improvement (exit 0)\" and a test asserting\n`stale=0` exactly — individually correct, jointly contradictory; reducing complexity of a\nbaselined function now passes `make lint` and fails CI (bug `dystopian-bardlike-basil`).\n\nWhy review missed it, measured on the code-v3 sidecar corpus (1881 sidecars / 1243 changes /\n3384 surfaced findings; replay harness reproduces stored v3 priorities 0/3384 mismatch):\n- **Pass-1 recall gap**: the `tests` criterion's change-detector litmus is refactor-based; an\n  assertion that breaks on a legitimate future *improvement* matches no antipattern.\n- **Pass-3 scoring gap**: test findings land in the maintainability lane, whose multiplier is\n  churn90 — absent on 80% of findings, and absent ⇒ ×0.5 (a data gap penalized as low\n  frequency). The dominant binary (`reachable_path_without_automated_coverage`, moderate 0.6)\n  therefore caps at priority ~0.30. Meanwhile Pass-2's already-answered `prod_impact` /\n  `trigger_likelihood` / `likelihood` are collected and DISCARDED for that lane — and they\n  separate the corpus cleanly: 1120/1664 tests findings are prod=none/low internal-edge gaps\n  (correctly advisory); the prod=medium/high tail (70) is uniformly load-bearing.\n- **Posture gap**: `tests` is advisory@0.95, blocking_enabled=false — even a found, verified,\n  consequential finding cannot block.\n\n## Approach\nThree coupled changes (one deliverable: give the tests dimension recall AND calibrated teeth):\n\n1. **Pass-1 recall** — add a \"contract-contradicting assertion\" antipattern to the shipped\n   `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md`: flag a test/assert that forbids a state the\n   same diff's contract (docstring / exit-code semantics / commit message) explicitly declares\n   allowed. Finding must quote BOTH halves verbatim. Guards: a stated deliberate tightening is\n   not flagged; exact-value asserts on pure functions stay valid (existing guard iv).\n2. **Pass-2 vocabulary** — (a) new serious maintainability binary\n   `forbids_contract_allowed_state` in `CodeSeverityAttrs` + the Pass-2 verify prompt\n   (both-halves-verbatim evidence; stated intent to tighten ⇒ FALSE). (b) Re-scope the\n   `prod_impact` and `trigger_likelihood` field descriptions in BOTH\n   `code-review-verify.md` and `verify_models.py` — today they are documented as scoping the\n   PRODUCTION consequence only; amend each to state it also keys the maintainability lane's\n   user-reach damping (for a coverage/contract finding, `prod_impact` = the user-facing reach\n   of the path the missing test / broken contract guards; `trigger_likelihood` = how often a\n   user-reachable action exercises that path). The corpus crosstab shows verifiers already\n   answer them this way for maint findings; the amendment makes the existing behavior the\n   documented contract.\n3. **Pass-3 impact model code-v4** (`impact_code`, ADR 0036 version bump) — split the maint\n   lane by binary class:\n   - serious consequence (`unversioned_published_contract_break`,\n     `safety_net_removal_without_replacement`, `forbids_contract_allowed_state`): undamped ×1.0;\n   - moderate consequence (`contract_drift`, `hidden_invariant`,\n     `reachable_path_without_automated_coverage`): × prod_impact multiplier\n     (high/medium=1.0, low=0.6, none=0.5) × 0.75 when trigger_likelihood=rare — the\n     user-reach keying;\n   - debt (`implicit_coupling`, `dead_code`): churn multiplier becomes AMPLIFIER-ONLY\n     (1.0 + 0.5·min(churn90,30)/30 ∈ [1.0,1.5]; operator decision 2026-08-19: churn may only\n     increase impact, never diminish it). Churn stays out of the consequence lanes so hot-file\n     prod=none nits cannot climb into the block zone.\n   - **reversibility floor restricted to the consequence lanes** (prod + serious/moderate\n     maint): today's floor is lane-blind, so a minor debt binary on a hard_to_reverse surface\n     would floor to 0.6 and cross tests@0.54 — defeating the debt-cannot-block invariant. In\n     v4 the 0.6 floor applies only when a consequence-lane binary contributed (consequence\n     base > 0 AND hard_to_reverse_surface); the debt lane never floors. Corpus replay is\n     identical under this restriction (163/99), and the 4 existing debt-only+hard-to-reverse\n     findings stay advisory.\n   Prod lane tiers/trigger multipliers and detection amp: unchanged. priority=validity×impact:\n   unchanged.\n4. **Routing** — flip `tests` to blocking@0.54 in the packaged `criteria_routing.json`\n   (operator-approved 2026-08-19); update the governance-pin tests to the 8-member blocking set.\n\nCorpus grounding (full replay, see ticket comment for tables): v3 today blocks 42/1243 changes\n(3.4%); v4 + tests@0.54 blocks 99 (8.0% — operator-accepted). Zero demotions of currently-\nblocking findings; newly-blocking hand-samples are uniformly consequential; no docs/cosmetic\nentries; the prod=none/low internal-edge mass stays advisory (~0.27–0.30). No additional\nvalidity floor (0.85–0.95 band hand-read as true positives; the existing val<0.5 drop stands).\n\n**Stored sidecars are never rewritten.** The version bump gates scoring: reviews run after\nthis change emit `impact_model_version: \"code-v4\"`; existing code-v3 sidecar files are not\nre-scored or mutated in place (the 42→99 replay is an offline analysis, not a migration).\n\n## Recorded verdicts (acceptance criteria of the original framing)\n- **Mechanism**: extension of the existing `tests` criterion + Pass-2 vocabulary + Pass-3\n  code-v4 rescoring — NOT a new standalone criterion (gate survey found the contradiction shape\n  is a one-off) and NOT a \"gates must leave a sanctioned path\" plan-review rule (no independent\n  instance; would require simulating future contributor workflows — FP-prone).\n- **Distinction from rejected `ci-gate-compat`** (`unaroused-undead-ibisbill`): that criterion\n  demanded compat mechanisms for external in-flight branches, where rebase-and-fix is the\n  remedy. This checks INTERNAL self-consistency of one diff against its own stated contract,\n  where no contributor remedy exists — a coherence check, not a compat ramp.\n- **Gate survey** (recorded in comment): complexity ratchet is the only shipped gate with the\n  shape; module-size, commit-trailer, DCO, bugfix-size, region gates are clean.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py` (impact_code v4 incl. floor restriction),\n`verify_models.py` (new binary + re-scoped prod_impact/trigger_likelihood descriptions),\n`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md` (new binary instruction + re-scoped field\ndescriptions) + `code-review-tests.md` (antipattern),\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` + `sidecar.py` (flip + version bump),\ngovernance-pin tests, code-review eval corpus, `docs/experiments/` (replay script + results).\n\n## Testing\n- Unit: impact_code v4 arithmetic — serious-maint undamped; prod_impact keying incl. none/low\n  dampening; amplifier-only churn floor at 1.0 (churn=0 ⇒ multiplier exactly 1.0, never 0.5);\n  reversibility floor fires for a consequence-lane binary on a hard_to_reverse surface but a\n  debt-only finding (dead_code/implicit_coupling) on a hard_to_reverse surface stays at its\n  debt score (max 0.45 — advisory under tests@0.54); absent-binary abstention unchanged.\n- Eval corpus: fire case from the `8eadb4fbc5` tolerance/assert pair; pass cases: a stated\n  deliberate tightening, and a pure-function exact-value assert (must not fire).\n- Replay: the corpus replay script re-run against the landed formula must reproduce the\n  recorded v4 would-block set (163 findings / 99 changes) byte-for-byte.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `impact_code` ships the code-v4 lane split above (incl. the consequence-lane-only\n      reversibility floor); `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION == \"code-v4\"`; stored code-v3 sidecar files\n      are not rewritten or re-scored in place; a sidecar lacking the new binary gets 0\n      contribution from it.\n- [ ] `forbids_contract_allowed_state` exists in `CodeSeverityAttrs` and the Pass-2 prompt with\n      both-halves-verbatim evidence and the deliberate-tightening guard; the\n      `prod_impact`/`trigger_likelihood` descriptions in both files state the maintainability\n      user-reach keying.\n- [ ] `code-review-tests.md` carries the contract-contradicting-assertion antipattern + guards.\n- [ ] Packaged routing: `tests` blocking@0.54 with a `_comment` citing this ticket + the replay;\n      governance-pin tests assert the new 8-member set.\n- [ ] Eval fire/pass cases above pass the code-review eval spec.\n- [ ] Replay script + results committed under `docs/experiments/`; re-run reproduces the\n      recorded would-block set (163 findings / 99 changes), and a debt-only+hard_to_reverse\n      finding scores advisory."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787192960011270001,"uuid":"1ca57820-5b02-448b-a7d3-a69dd31c83f3"}